{"c": null, "r": "I'm designing a Bank class where each instance maintains its own accounts dictionary to ensure instances don't share state. I'm creating a custom exception for insufficient funds, then building out the core methods like opening accounts, depositing, and withdrawing money with proper validation—checking that initial balances are non-negative and amounts are positive integers.

For the withdraw and transfer operations, I'm validating that both source and destination accounts exist before attempting any balance changes, so unknown accounts raise KeyError before any mutations occur. I'm being careful about the order of checks: validating amounts first, then checking accounts exist, then checking for sufficient funds, so that failed operations leave balances unchanged.
", "t": [["write_file", "{"path":"D:\\Projects\\local_ai\\strata-lab\\runs\\work\\hermes\\bank-1794053343\\bank.py","content":"\"\"\"Account helpers. Balances are integer cents.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass InsufficientFunds(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when a withdrawal or transfer exceeds the source balance.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass Bank:\n    \"\"\"A set of named accounts with integer-cent balances.\n\n    Each Bank owns its accounts; two instances never share state.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._accounts = {}\n\n    def open_account(self, name, initial=0):\n        if initial < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"initial must be >= 0: {!r}\".format(initial))\n        if name in self._accounts:\n            raise ValueError(\"account exists: \" + str(name))\n        self._accounts[name] = initial\n\n    def deposit(self, name, amount):\n        if amount <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"amount must be > 0: {!r}\".format(amount))\n        self._require(name)\n        self._accounts[name] += amount\n\n    def withdraw(self, name, amount):\n        if amount <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"amount must be > 0: {!r}\".format(amount))\n        current = self._require(name)\n        if current < amount:\n            raise InsufficientFunds(\n                \"account {!r} balance {} < {}\".format(name, current, amount))\n        self._accounts[name] = current - amount\n\n    def balance(self, name):\n        return self._require(name)\n\n    def transfer(self, src, dst, amount):\n        if amount <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"amount must be > 0: {!r}\".format(amount))\n        if src == dst:\n            raise ValueError(\"cannot transfer to the same account: \" + str(src))\n        src_balance = self._require(src)\n        dst_balance = self._require(dst)\n        if src_balance < amount:\n            raise InsufficientFunds(\n                \"account {!r} balance {} < {}\".format(src, src_balance, amount))\n        self._accounts[src] = src_balance - amount\n        self._accounts[dst] = dst_balance + amount\n\n    def _require(self, name):\n        try:\n            return self._accounts[name]\n        except KeyError:\n            raise KeyError(name)\n\n\ndefault_bank = Bank()\n\n\ndef open_account(name, initial=0):\n    return default_bank.open_account(name, initial)\n\n\ndef deposit(name, amount):\n    return default_bank.deposit(name, amount)\n\n\ndef withdraw(name, amount):\n    return default_bank.withdraw(name, amount)\n\n\ndef balance(name):\n    return default_bank.balance(name)\n\n\ndef transfer(src, dst, amount):\n    return default_bank.transfer(src, dst, amount)\n"}"]]}

